# Keeps the build context to source. Everything here is either rebuilt inside the
# image or has no business in one.

# Build output. Copying a host bin/ or obj/ into the image is worse than wasteful:
# obj/ carries project.assets.json pinned to host paths, and a restore that finds
# it may skip work it needed to do, producing an image built against whatever the
# last local build resolved.
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Test projects. They are not published into any service image, and leaving them
# out keeps a test-only package out of the context entirely.
tests/

# Local developer configuration. appsettings.Development.json carries a local
# connection string and would otherwise sit in the image alongside the real one,
# where the only thing keeping it from being read is the environment name.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/*.user
**/.vs/
**/.idea/

# Secrets, in case one is ever written here by mistake. This is belt and braces —
# nothing in this repository writes these — but the cost of the line is nothing
# and the cost of the omission is a credential in a published layer.
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12
**/*.key
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Version control and CI.
.git/
.github/
**/.gitignore
